#: ../../../how-to/shell-completions.rst:42
msgid "zsh, once you say so"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/shell-completions.rst:44
msgid ""
"bash and fish read their directories without further help. zsh needs the "
"directory on its ``fpath``, so add this to ``~/.zshrc`` ahead of the call to "
"``compinit``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/shell-completions.rst:47
msgid ""
"fpath+=(\"$(pipx environment --value PIPX_COMPLETION_DIR)/zsh/site-"
"functions\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/shell-completions.rst:51
msgid ""
"``pipx uninstall`` takes the links away, and ``pipx unexpose`` removes them "
"while leaving the package in place (see :doc:`expose-apps`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/shell-completions.rst:56
msgid "Ship completions from your package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/shell-completions.rst:58
msgid ""
"Install completion scripts through your build backend's data files. With "
"setuptools:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/shell-completions.rst:60
msgid ""
"setup(\n"
"    name=\"your-tool\",\n"
"    data_files=[\n"
"        (\"share/bash-completion/completions\", [\"completions/your-"
"tool\"]),\n"
"        (\"share/zsh/site-functions\", [\"completions/_your-tool\"]),\n"
"        (\"share/fish/vendor_completions.d\", [\"completions/your-tool."
"fish\"]),\n"
"    ],\n"
")"
msgstr ""

